======

Which one should you choose?

| Your Requirement                         | Recommended Starting Point                       |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| Learning and experimenting               | **2B**                                           |
| Lightweight custom tuning                | **2B base model**                                |
| Simple chatbot                           | **2B-IT**                                        |
| Better business chatbot                  | **9B-IT**                                        |
| Fine-tuning for a specialized task       | **9B or 27B base model**, depending on resources |
| Large, demanding text task               | **27B / 27B-IT**                                 |
| Direct user interaction and instructions | Choose an **`-IT`** version                      |


========

B = Billion Parameters
IT = Instruction Tuned

2B  = Small
9B  = Medium
27B = Large

Base = Customize / Fine-tune
IT   = Ready to follow instructions

=========


For your current Vertex AI fine-tuning lesson, if you are learning how to create a specialized model from your own examples,
the base model is useful for understanding tuning. If your goal is mainly to build a chatbot that directly responds to users, 
an -IT model is generally the more natural starting point. Google also recommends considering prompting first when it can achieve the desired behavior before investing in tuning.

